From: A333 SDK <a333@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] obexd: regenerate builtin plugins after configuration changes

An incremental Buildroot reconfiguration from --disable-obex to
--enable-obex can retain an empty obexd/src/builtin.h generated by the
previous configuration. Source file timestamps do not invalidate it, so
obexd exits with "No service driver registered" despite compiled plugins.

Depend on the configured Makefile so the builtin list follows the active
configuration, including changes to experimental plugins.

Upstream: pending
Signed-off-by: A333 SDK <a333@example.invalid>
---
 Makefile.obexd | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile.obexd b/Makefile.obexd
--- a/Makefile.obexd
+++ b/Makefile.obexd
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ BUILT_SOURCES += obexd/src/builtin.h
 
 obexd/src/plugin.$(OBJEXT): obexd/src/builtin.h
 
-obexd/src/builtin.h: obexd/src/genbuiltin $(obexd_builtin_sources)
+obexd/src/builtin.h: Makefile obexd/src/genbuiltin $(obexd_builtin_sources)
 	$(AM_V_at)$(MKDIR_P) $(dir $@)
 	$(AM_V_GEN)$(srcdir)/obexd/src/genbuiltin $(obexd_builtin_modules) > $@
 
